{% extends "tutorial_base.html.j2" %}

{% block tutorial_body %}
        <!-- Intro Card -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card">
          <h2>Instant Version Verification &amp; Release Notes</h2>
          <p>
            Whether you are verifying that your shop station is running the latest CAM solver update, checking what new post-processor or CAD unfolding features were added in a recent release, or copying system diagnostics for support, the built-in <strong>About RotaryCAM</strong> dialog provides full build provenance and a chronological changelog in one click.
          </p>
          <div class="doc-intro-grid">
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Build Provenance</span>
              <span class="value">Version, Git Commit &amp; UTC Build Date</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">What Changed</span>
              <span class="value">Built-In Release Notes &amp; Feature Highlights</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Support Export</span>
              <span class="value">One-Click <code class="mono">📋 Copy Diagnostics</code></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 1
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-1">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 01</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Click <code class="mono">ⓘ About</code> in the Top-Right Header Bar</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              From anywhere in the RotaryCAM workspace, look at the top-right application header bar (next to <code class="mono">⚙ Machines</code>):
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Click the <span class="ui-chip">ⓘ About</span> button in the top-right navigation bar (you can also click the version badge in the bottom-right status bar).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 1 — Clicking 'ⓘ About' in the top-right header bar</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <img src="assets/changelog-1-open-about.png" alt="Step 1: Clicking the About button in the top-right header bar of RotaryCAM" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 2
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-2">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 02</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Inspect Build Metadata, Release Changelog &amp; Copy Diagnostics</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              The <strong>About RotaryCAM</strong> modal opens over the workspace and is divided into three sections:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>1. Build Metadata Table (Top):</strong> Displays the active <strong>Version</strong> (<code class="mono">v1.0.0</code>), exact <strong>Git Commit</strong> hash, <strong>Build Date (UTC)</strong>, <strong>CI Build Run ID</strong>, host <strong>Platform</strong> (<code class="mono">darwin/arm64</code>), <strong>Build Mode</strong>, and current <strong>License Status</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>2. What Changed — Recent Highlights (Center):</strong> A scrollable, date-stamped engineering changelog detailing newly shipped capabilities—such as <em>Simultaneous X/Y/A Pre-Pierce Positioning in G93 Mode</em>, <em>Tube Bending Quota &amp; License Support</em>, <em>3D Bent Tube "Cut-and-Bend" Unfolding</em>, <em>Straight HSS Cheek Cuts &amp; 5-Zone Corner Relief</em>, <em>Multi-Stick Nesting <code class="mono">.zip</code> Export</em>, and <em>SimCNC 3.5 vs. 3.6 Beta Profiles</em>.</li>
              <li><strong>3. Copy Diagnostics (Bottom-Right):</strong> Click <span class="ui-chip emerald">📋 Copy Diagnostics</span> to copy a formatted snapshot of your build metadata and environment to the clipboard when reporting an issue or requesting support.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 2 — The About RotaryCAM modal showing build metadata, recent changelog highlights, and Copy Diagnostics</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <img src="assets/changelog-2-modal.png" alt="Step 2: About RotaryCAM modal displaying build metadata, release changelog, and Copy Diagnostics button" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
          </figure>

          <!-- Changelog Transcript Section -->
          <div class="doc-step-body" id="release-transcript" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
              <span>🗓️</span> Current Release Changelog Entries
            </h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
              The built-in changelog view reflects all recent production engine updates. Below is the full transcript of recent engineering releases directly from the application:
            </p>

            <!-- Latest Release: Oct 22 -->
            <div style="background: rgba(20, 23, 29, 0.95); border: 1px solid var(--surface-border); border-left: 3px solid var(--plasma-amber); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); padding-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                <span class="mono" style="color: var(--plasma-amber); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem;">🗓️ Oct 22, 2026</span>
                <span style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.82rem;">Full-Speed HSS Flat Walls, Corner Tracking, Hypertherm SYNC Cut Charts &amp; Feature Toggles</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                <li><strong>Full-Speed Square &amp; Rectangular Tube Flat Walls &amp; Clean Lead-Ins:</strong> Torch motion now accelerates smoothly back up to full cutting speed across the flat faces of square and rectangular HSS tubing between corner rotations&mdash;preventing overheated walls, wide kerfs, and heavy low-speed dross&mdash;while straight flat-face lead-ins are emitted as a single clean move without tiny micro-steps.</li>
                <li><strong>Smooth HSS Corner Rotations &amp; Clean SimCNC 3.6 G93 Corner Tracking:</strong> Fixed a Z-axis height spike on square and rectangular HSS tube corners so the torch glides smoothly around every corner fillet at constant standoff without lifting or jerking mid-corner. Updated the <strong>SimCNC 3.6 Beta (G93 Inverse-Time)</strong> machine profile to track HSS corners perpendicular to the radius by default, eliminating corner-exit bevel lag and flat-face Y-axis overshoot.</li>
                <li><strong>Built-In Hypertherm SYNC Rev 4 Cut Charts &amp; Smart Cartridge Recommendation:</strong> Built-in factory Hypertherm Powermax 45/65/85/105 SYNC Rev 4 (<code class="mono">810500MU</code>) cut chart library covering 552 presets across Standard Best Quality, Standard High Prod, FineCut High Speed, and FineCut Low Speed consumables in both Metric and Imperial units for Mild Steel, Stainless Steel, and Aluminum. Features automatic cartridge amperage recommendation for thin-wall vs. thick-wall stock with out-of-range warnings and 1-click cartridge switching, automatically matching feedrate, kerf width, pierce height, pierce delay, cut height, arc voltage, and gas pressure to the part's detected wall thickness as soon as a STEP file is loaded.</li>
                <li><strong>Dedicated Cut Charts Manager &amp; Manual Overrides:</strong> Dedicated Cut Charts Manager UI (separate from Machine Settings) where operators can add custom material thicknesses, tweak feedrates and kerf widths, or reset to factory Hypertherm tables. Explicit per-session Manual Override in the sidebar with one-click reset back to the thickness-matched chart preset.</li>
                <li><strong>Selective Feature Enable/Disable in Single Part Inspection:</strong> Operators can now check or uncheck individual holes, slots, notches, cutouts, or scribe marks in Single Part Inspection to skip them in the generated G-code (for both single parts and full-stick pack nesting) without modifying the CAD model. Start and end tube sever cuts are permanently locked on so parts always sever cleanly from the mill stick.</li>
                <li><strong>Configurable Heat-Optimized vs. One-Direction Cut Ordering:</strong> Operators can choose between automatic thermal hedging (staggering internal holes and slots across the tube to prevent heat warping) or strict one-direction monotonic cutting from free-end to chuck.</li>
                <li><strong>Clean Lead-Out M5 Torch-Off &amp; Immediate Safe-Z Retract:</strong> <code class="mono">M5</code> torch-off now fires cleanly at the end of the lead-out immediately before lifting to safe Z height, eliminating brief post-<code class="mono">M5</code> motion at cut height.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- Oct 20 Release -->
            <div style="background: rgba(20, 23, 29, 0.95); border: 1px solid var(--surface-border); border-left: 3px solid var(--cyan-arc); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); padding-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                <span class="mono" style="color: var(--cyan-arc); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem;">🗓️ Oct 20, 2026</span>
                <span style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.82rem;">Cut-and-Bend Unfolding, Flat HSS Projection &amp; Multi-Stick ZIP</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                <li><strong>Simultaneous X/Y/A Pre-Pierce Positioning in G93 Mode:</strong> On controllers supporting native G93 inverse-time feedrates (such as SimCNC 3.6), positioning moves between features now travel in X, Y, and A simultaneously in a single coordinated move rather than stopping between separate linear rapid and rotary indexing steps, while preserving split positioning for G94 controllers.</li>
                <li><strong>Tube Bending Quota &amp; License Support:</strong> Added per-file and hourly bend entitlements across guest, signed-in, and licensed shop tiers (3 bends per STEP file for guests, 10 bends/hour for signed-in accounts, and 100 bends by default on customer licenses).</li>
                <li><strong>3D Bent Tube &ldquo;Cut-and-Bend&rdquo; Unfolding:</strong> Automatic spine detection and unfolding of bent round pipes and square/rectangular HSS into straight-stock pie-cut relief patterns with an uncut extrados living hinge.</li>
                <li><strong>Straight HSS Cheek Cuts &amp; 5-Zone Corner Relief:</strong> True-plane projection onto flat HSS walls (<code class="mono">projectContourOntoHSSSurface</code>) eliminating wavy bend lines on flat faces, with configurable relief cut counts, spine width, and inner-wall binding clearance.</li>
                <li><strong>3D Bent Toolpath Preview &amp; Collapsible Bend Groups:</strong> Renders relief toolpaths directly onto the 3D bent tube mesh and groups relief cuts under interactive <code class="mono">Bend #N</code> rows.</li>
                <li><strong>Multi-Stick Nesting .zip Export:</strong> Direct <code class="mono">📦 Download ZIP (N Sticks)</code> buttons in the Pack toolbar, Stick Pager, and G-Code header with automatic G-code refresh on nesting edits.</li>
                <li><strong>SimCNC 3.5 vs 3.6 Beta Profiles &amp; Instant Solid Matching:</strong> Dedicated <em>SimCNC 3.5 (G94 + G93 Emulation)</em> and <em>SimCNC 3.6 Beta (G93 Inverse-Time)</em> machine presets with seamless WebGL preservation on profile switch.</li>
                <li><strong>Configurable X-Axis Travel &amp; Start Direction:</strong> Added <em>Workpiece Moves on X (<code class="mono">G92 X-L &rarr; X0</code>, free-end to chuck)</em> vs <em>Torch Moves on X (<code class="mono">G92 X0 &rarr; +max(X)</code>)</em> origin mode in machine kinematics, defaulting SimCNC profiles to workpiece-moving X.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- Oct 19 Release -->
            <div style="background: rgba(20, 23, 29, 0.95); border: 1px solid var(--surface-border); border-left: 3px solid var(--cyan-arc); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); padding-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                <span class="mono" style="color: var(--cyan-arc); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem;">🗓️ Oct 19, 2026</span>
                <span style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.82rem;">Standalone Offline Bundles &amp; Persistent Workspace</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                <li><strong>Cross-Platform Offline Releases (Windows, macOS, Linux):</strong> Self-contained single-binary distribution (<code class="mono">RotaryCAM</code>) with embedded web assets and 100% offline Ed25519 license activation.</li>
                <li><strong>Persistent Session History:</strong> Automatically saves and restores processed STEP models, solid selections, and generated G-code across restarts.</li>
                <li><strong>Version &amp; Build Diagnostics:</strong> Added the About dialog with Git commit hash, CI run ID, and one-click diagnostic clipboard export.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- Oct 16 Release -->
            <div style="background: rgba(20, 23, 29, 0.95); border: 1px solid var(--surface-border); border-left: 3px solid var(--emerald-cut); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); padding-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                <span class="mono" style="color: var(--emerald-cut); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem;">🗓️ Oct 16, 2026</span>
                <span style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.82rem;">G93 Inverse-Time Precision &amp; 3D Stock Preview</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                <li><strong>G93 Inverse-Time &amp; Dynamic THC Refinements:</strong> Eliminated circular lead-in/out micro-sliver feedrate spikes, unified G93/G94 preambles across Single-Part and Pack Mode, and deduplicated HSS corner THC lock macros.</li>
                <li><strong>3D Uncut Stock Envelope &amp; Simulator Plunge Fix:</strong> Added translucent 3D stock overlays and accurate SimCNC <code class="mono">M3</code> vertical pierce-to-cut plunge in the 3D simulator.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
{% endblock %}
